<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31224" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρω</span></b>  (B), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>say, speak, tell</i>:—
				Act.
			 is used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, and in <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνηστῆρσιν δ᾽ . . τάδε εἴρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.162
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				13.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δέ τοι νημερτέα εἴρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.137
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 in same sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ εἴρετο δεύτερον αὖτις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.513
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴροντο δὲ κήδε᾽ ἑκάστη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.542
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				359
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 3sg.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρεται</span>
			<i>is said</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				172
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				261
			</span></i>: for other forms 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῶ.</span>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝέρ</span>-y<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ω</span>, fr. root of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῶ</span>,
		q.v.)</div>
